note: we use G54 as coordinate system
check the cam jobs. see CAM_CHECKLIST
export the cam jobs using the postprocess_all.py macro. It postprocesses all jobs (you have to click ok for each of them), then runs fixjobs.sh
 fixjob.sh changes S100 to P100 on M3 commands, and changes Z operations to laser on and laser off in the engraving job.
you probably want to link scripts/postprocess_all.py to your local macro folder

0. preparing fixer holes on stock
This creates four 4mm dia holes at ({40,50},{0,300})
This is to put holes for screws on the right places on my SnapMaker 2 in order to fix the stock to nuts in the table.
Mill: stockprepare.gcode
stock size: x>90mm y>330 mm z~=21mm z<24mm 
origo is x=-40mm,y=0mm from the left bottom hole, aka ~15mm left to the edge of stock
clearance height is 100mm for this job.


1. Fedél
stock size: x>90mm y>280mm z~=21mm z<24mm (+ where you fix it)
1.0 Laser: cross.gcode
set x=0 y=0 relative to the part, z=top of the stock+ ~[3-5] mm
1.1 Laser: gravir-fixed.gcode
set the origo x=-15mm,y=-10mm from the center of the cross, same height as before
1.2 Mill: box.gcode
use 3.175 endmill
set the origo x=-15mm,y=-10mm from the center of the cross, on the bottom
1.3 Mill: fedel-alja.gcode
use 3.175 endmill
turn the stock bottom-up (x'=-x,y'=y)
use the bottom-left screw hole for x-y calibration. move x-30mm,y-20mm, set z at bottom of the stock
set the origo there
2. Alja
stock size: x>90mm y>280mm z~=21mm z<24mm (+ where you fix it)
2.1 Mill: alja.gcode
set the origo x=-15mm,y=-10mm from the bottom left corner of the part, on the bottom
3. Eleje-vége
stock size: x>90mm y>163mm z~=20mm z<24mm (+ where you fix it)
3.1 Mill: eleje-vege.gcode
set the origo x=-15mm,y=-10mm from the bottom left corner of the part, on the bottom

